  "full_response": "Sample Git Commit Message:\n```\nRefactor: Move hardcoded credentials to environment variables\n\n- Removed hardcoded credentials from source code\n- Added references to existing environment variables for API keys and database connection strings\n- Updated documentation for future maintenance and best practices\n\nImprovements:\n- Enhances security by avoiding hardcoded sensitive information\n- Simplifies deployment process by making use of environment variables\n- Adheres to the best practices for managing secrets\n```\n\nSample File Diff (Before):\n```diff\n// config.js\nconst API_KEY = \"12345-ABCDE\";\nconst DB_CONNECTION_STRING = \"mysql://user:pass@localhost/dbname\";\n```\n\nSample File Diff (After):\n```diff\n// config.js\nconst API_KEY = process.env.API_KEY;\nconst DB_CONNECTION_STRING = process.env.DB_CONNECTION_STRING;\n\n// Documentation Update\n// Make sure to set the API_KEY and DB_CONNECTION_STRING environment variables before starting the application\n```\n\nThis shows the removal of hardcoded API key and database connection string credentials from the source code and their replacement with references to environment variables. Additionally, it includes a commitment to update documentation for future maintenance and best practices.",
